# blocks per SM unchanged; bits unchanged (ubatch dump md5 equal to the base's, twice). The q3tail
# sum model (a warp pair's step = tensor + issue + barriers) at 1.46-1.60 GHz gives the window
# -15.6..-19.5 ms at P = 4096 [derived] of ~510 ms: pp4096 8,024 -> 8,277..8,343. At P = 512 flash
# is ~1.8 ms of ~75 ms and the model gives ~-0.3 ms: a screen for 0.
kind: ab
question: does the flash instruction diet shorten the Qwen3 prompt as the q3tail sum model says?
term: pp tok/s @ P = 4096, n = 0, A6000, Qwen3-30B-A3B Q4_K_M - (q3fa - base) / base, paired by
  round
unit: %
predict: +3.0..+4.2
rounds: 3
